---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Browse Camera Lenses – Camera Central"
  description="Explore camera lenses by system and find the right fit for your setup."
>
  <div class="w-full max-w-5xl mx-auto space-y-8">
    <section class="rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-8 shadow-sm">
      <p class="text-sm font-medium text-gray-500">Lenses</p>
      <h1 class="mt-2 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-gray-900">
        Browse lenses by system
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-gray-600">
        Explore lens ecosystems and find lenses that fit your camera system. Start with the brand
        you shoot with, then browse by category, price, and weight.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-4">
        <a
          href="/find"
          class="inline-flex items-center rounded-xl border border-gray-300 bg-white px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-gray-900 transition hover:bg-gray-50"
        >
          Take the quiz
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2 xl:grid-cols-3">
      <a
        href="/lenses/canon-rf"
        class="group rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm transition hover:border-gray-300 hover:bg-gray-50"
        style="cursor:pointer;"
      >
        <p class="text-sm font-medium text-gray-500">Canon Mirrorless</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900">Canon RF / RF-S</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-gray-600">
          Native Canon mirrorless lenses for cameras like the R50, R10, R7, R8, R6 Mark II, and R5.
        </p>

        <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 text-sm text-gray-700">
          <li>RF full-frame lenses</li>
          <li>RF-S APS-C lenses</li>
          <li>Best for modern Canon mirrorless systems</li>
        </ul>

        <span class="mt-5 inline-flex items-center text-sm font-medium text-gray-900">
          Explore RF lenses →
        </span>
      </a>

      <a
        href="/lenses/canon-ef"
        class="group rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm transition hover:border-gray-300 hover:bg-gray-50"
        style="cursor:pointer;"
      >
        <p class="text-sm font-medium text-gray-500">Canon DSLR / Adapted</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900">Canon EF / EF-S</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-gray-600">
          Canon DSLR lenses, including full-frame EF and APS-C EF-S options. Many can also be adapted to RF bodies.
        </p>

        <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 text-sm text-gray-700">
          <li>EF full-frame DSLR lenses</li>
          <li>EF-S APS-C DSLR lenses</li>
          <li>Great for legacy Canon setups</li>
        </ul>

        <span class="mt-5 inline-flex items-center text-sm font-medium text-gray-900">
          Explore EF lenses →
        </span>
      </a>

      <a
        href="/lenses/sony-e"
        class="group rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm transition hover:border-gray-300 hover:bg-gray-50"
        style="cursor:pointer;"
      >
        <p class="text-sm font-medium text-gray-500">Sony Mirrorless</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900">Sony E</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-gray-600">
          Sony E-mount lenses for APS-C and full-frame Sony mirrorless cameras, including native and third-party options.
        </p>

        <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 text-sm text-gray-700">
          <li>APS-C and full-frame options</li>
          <li>Strong Sigma and Tamron support</li>
          <li>One of the largest mirrorless ecosystems</li>
        </ul>

        <span class="mt-5 inline-flex items-center text-sm font-medium text-gray-900">
          Explore Sony E lenses →
        </span>
      </a>

      <a
        href="/lenses/nikon-z"
        class="group rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm transition hover:border-gray-300 hover:bg-gray-50"
        style="cursor:pointer;"
      >
        <p class="text-sm font-medium text-gray-500">Nikon Mirrorless</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900">Nikon Z</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-gray-600">
          Nikon Z-mount lenses for APS-C and full-frame Nikon mirrorless cameras, including native Nikon glass and select third-party options.
        </p>

        <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 text-sm text-gray-700">
          <li>Z full-frame and DX APS-C lenses</li>
          <li>Clean modern mirrorless system</li>
          <li>Strong upgrade path within Nikon Z</li>
        </ul>

        <span class="mt-5 inline-flex items-center text-sm font-medium text-gray-900">
          Explore Nikon Z lenses →
        </span>
      </a>

      <a
        href="/lenses/fujifilm-x"
        class="group rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm transition hover:border-gray-300 hover:bg-gray-50"
        style="cursor:pointer;"
      >
        <p class="text-sm font-medium text-gray-500">Fujifilm Mirrorless</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900">Fujifilm X</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-gray-600">
          Fujifilm X-mount lenses for APS-C Fuji mirrorless cameras, including native Fuji lenses and third-party alternatives.
        </p>

        <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 text-sm text-gray-700">
          <li>APS-C-focused system</li>
          <li>Strong travel and photography identity</li>
          <li>Great Sigma and Viltrox value options</li>
        </ul>

        <span class="mt-5 inline-flex items-center text-sm font-medium text-gray-900">
          Explore Fujifilm X lenses →
        </span>
      </a>
    </section>

    <section class="rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 bg-gray-50 p-6">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">How lens compatibility works</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700">
        Not every lens fits every camera body. Some fit directly, some need an adapter, and some may
        force crop mode or only make sense within a specific sensor format. Camera Central keeps
        compatibility front and center so it is easier to build the right camera system.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>